The README.md hunk from PR #6949 is dropped. .dockerignore excludes *.md from
the build context, so scripts/apply-patches.sh runs against a tree with no
README.md and the hunk fails the build — while a local dry-run passes, because
the file is there. The dropped hunk only documented the new
RELAY_RESPONSE_HEADER_TIMEOUT variable; .env.example is not excluded and is
kept. Re-download pull/6949.diff and you get the README.md hunk back.

Downloaded as pull/6949.diff, not .patch: the PR has two commits and the second
edits lines the first wrote, which `patch -p1` cannot walk.

